1. Scope and permitted use

This license applies to the programs, skill documentation, templates, and examples in Novel OS that teateatea03 has the right to license. Third-party materials remain subject to their original licenses; see THIRD_PARTY.md. This license does not restrict rights granted by those licenses.

Anyone complying with this license may use, copy, modify, and redistribute the system. Noncommercial use is free. Commercial use requires acceptance of and compliance with the profit-sharing terms below. Redistribution of original or modified versions must retain this license, copyright notices, and third-party notices. Modified versions remain under the same terms of this license and must clearly identify modifications. A modified version must not be represented as the original author's unmodified version.

2. Scope of commercial profit sharing

Commercial users must pay 0.5% of the annual positive net profit from related products, services, and novels generated through use of this system or its modified versions. The calculation excludes other works, products, services, and unrelated business that did not use this system.

For each calendar year, aggregate the actual revenue from all related items and deduct refunds and actual, reasonable, attributable costs, expenses, and taxes. No revenue or cost may be counted twice. Unrelated business expenses are excluded, and this profit-sharing payment itself is not deducted before the calculation. Shared costs are allocated using the user's consistent and reasonable accounting method.

When the aggregate annual net profit is greater than zero, the amount payable is the annual related net profit multiplied by 0.005. No profit-sharing payment is due when the aggregate is zero or a loss. Losses may not be carried across years. Existing related works, products, or services that continue to generate positive net profit in later years remain subject to this calculation. Stopping use of the tools does not automatically remove the profit-sharing obligations for those existing related items. Newly created items that do not use this system are not included merely for that reason.

The obligations are borne by the user who actually uses this system and accepts the commercial terms. Publishers, clients, or readers do not automatically become payment obligors by receiving a work. When a novelist independently licenses a work to a publisher, the author's net profit is calculated from the related revenue received by the author; the publisher's unrelated sales or profits are not treated as the author's revenue.

3. Annual reporting and payment

The accounting period is the calendar year, January 1 through December 31. Users must self-report and pay the previous year's profit-sharing amount by March 31 of the following year. The report lists related items, revenue, total reasonable costs and taxes, net profit, and the profit-sharing amount. A short report is sufficient when there is no positive net profit.

Convert foreign currencies to US dollars using the user's consistent accounting exchange rate, and state the exchange-rate source and date used in the report. Each US dollar payable is paid with 1 USDT or 1 USDC on the BNB Smart Chain mainnet (BSC, chain ID 56). The payer bears the network transfer fees. This is a payment-denomination agreement, not a guarantee of stablecoin market prices, reserves, or redeemability. The receiving address and accepted Binance-Peg token contracts are listed in docs/COMMERCIAL_TERMS.md. Before paying, confirm the token, network, contract, and receiving details; do not treat a token contract as the receiving address.

4. Honest reporting and explicit acceptance

Before commercial use, the user must explicitly indicate acceptance of “Novel OS Source-Available and Commercial Profit-Sharing License 1.0” (Novel OS 原始碼公開與商業分潤授權 1.0) and retain a written or electronic record. Merely browsing the source code does not constitute acceptance of a payment contract. Users may first contact the maintainer through a GitHub issue containing no financial information to confirm the accepted version and a private reporting channel. Do not post financial summaries, payment information, or private works in public issues.

Profit sharing is based on honest self-reporting; it is not a voluntary donation. The system does not add hidden telemetry, automatic debiting, or compulsory auditing features for this purpose. Users will be contacted first if clarification is needed. Reports use only necessary information, which the maintainer must keep confidential. Unrelated business information or novel manuscripts are not required. Information that must be disclosed by law is handled in accordance with applicable law.

5. Rights in works and third-party rights

Using Novel OS does not make the user's novels, characters, worldbuilding, or other outputs the property of teateatea03. This license does not require transfer or joint ownership of those rights. Outputs do not automatically become modified versions of the system's programs merely because the tools were used. The commercial profit sharing above is a condition of use accepted by the user, not a claim that copyright in the tools naturally extends to every output. Users must still respect existing rights in works, third-party licenses, and the terms of the models or services used.

6. Redistribution and versions

Redistributors must make this license and the necessary third-party notices available to recipients, and may not accept the commercial payment terms on someone else's behalf. A later license version does not automatically replace this accepted version merely because the new version is published. Other uses may be separately agreed with teateatea03. Unless otherwise expressly agreed, this version applies.
